body:
Both AJAX fee-loading endpoints had no exception handling, so any DB runtime error (unhandled `PDOException`, missing column, etc.) printed an HTML error page. The browser's `fetch().then(r => r.json())` failed to parse that HTML, fell into `.catch()`, and showed the opaque "Network error. Please try again." alert.

## Changes

- **`get-student-fees.php` / `get-applicant-fees.php`** — Wrapped all logic in `try/catch(Throwable)`. Exceptions are now logged via `error_log()` and the response is a well-formed `{"error": "..."}` JSON with HTTP 500, which the existing JS `if (data.error)` branch handles gracefully.

```php
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    error_log('get-student-fees.php error: ' . $e->getMessage());
    http_response_code(500);
    echo json_encode(['error' => 'A server error occurred while loading student fees. Please contact your administrator.']);
}
```

- **`collect-payment.php`** — `$sms_enabled` was defined at line ~496 but first used at line ~435 inside the admission POST handler's success message, producing an undefined-variable warning. Moved the definition to before any POST handler and removed the now-duplicate assignment.

## Production note

If the new error message mentions an unknown column, the most likely pending migration is `admin/course-fees-move-global-to-program.sql`, which adds `bi_semester_start_month` / `tri_semester_start_month` to `cf_programs` — columns referenced by `acc_student_fee_summary()`.
